<!--PULL FROM GOOGLE CALENDAR -->

    <div id="cougar-events">


        <h2><a href="/events/">COUGAR <strong>EVENTS</strong></a></h2>
        <p><a style="display: inline-block; padding: 5px 10px; background-color: #006A99; border: none; border-radius: 5px; font-weight: bold; color: white; cursor: pointer;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/embed?src=honbjv24ogkg649udb0d8ki4m0%40group.calendar.google.com" target="_blank">See all events</a></p>
		
		

        
		
		            <p class="day-heading">Monday, November 16</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>12:00 am International Education Week</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-16 12:00 - 2026-11-21 12:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> </p>
						<p class="calendar-details"></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NDM5bGVtcnFwc3IyNmc1OHQ3c2VhcnRmN2EgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Tuesday, November 17</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>6:00 pm Visible Mending Class (Part 7 of 8)</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-17 06:00 - 2026-11-17 08:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Transform your holey clothing into a work of slow fashion art! Repairing and refurbishing your clothing keeps your clothing out of the waste stream, saves you money, gives you a creative outlet and will make you the envy of your friends. Join us for this eight-week exploration into the world of mending. We will be learning mending of socks, jeans and other pants, shirts and more types of clothing using techniques of weaving, embroidery, knitting, and more. Minimal sewing skills are required- we'll teach you what you need to know although some familiarity is useful.<br>Food Innovation Center<br><br><b>*Note:</b>This is an eight-week class. This class is part seven of eight.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NHE1dmIzcmRlZ2VwZDRyZTFta3U2N2Q1aW9fUjIwMjYxMDEzVDIyMDAwMCBob25ianYyNG9na2c2NDl1ZGIwZDhraTRtMEBn" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>6:30 pm Honorable Harvest Lecture Series: Practicing Our Way to Local</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-17 06:30 - 2026-11-17 07:30</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Culinary/Allied Health Building, 418 E Walnut St, Kalamazoo, MI 49007, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><p>PRACTICING OUR WAY TO LOCAL: NOTES AND LESSONS FROM THE FIELD</p><p><b>Culinary and Allied Health Building | Room 223<br>Presenter: Rachel Bair</b><br><br>Rachel Bair, the founding director of the Food Innovation Center, was granted a professional development leave in the late summer and early fall. She will spend it connecting with organizations and individuals who are actively gardening, cooking, organizing, advocating, and educating in the local food system in Kalamazoo and beyond. She will present what she has learned and share thoughts on where the movement is heading.</p><p><b>Registration Fee:</b>FREE</p><p><b>See More:</b><a href=https://valleyhub.kvcc.edu/events/honorable-harvest-lecture-series target=_blank><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>https://valleyhub.kvcc.edu/events/honorable-harvest-lecture-series</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a></p></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NjV0Y2d0NWZmamhoODJ0MTdpYnJkNG5tNjQgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Wednesday, November 18</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>10:00 am Bronco Bound</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 10:00 - 2026-11-18 02:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Are you interested in transferring to Western Michigan University after goal completion at Kalamazoo Valley? Whether you already know Western Michigan University is your choice, or are still exploring all of your options, Bronco Bound is for you! Come connect with WMU advisors and admissions representatives to get all of your questions answered. No appointment necessary! Stop by the transfer resource tables in the Texas Township Cafeteria anytime between 10 a.m. and 2 p.m.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NHJvb29lNDN2c2psbG1xOTVhcWhwZG1zOTYgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>11:00 am Art and Animation Club</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 11:00 - 2026-11-18 12:30</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Center for New Media, 100 E Michigan Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49007, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Come join a diverse group of students who love watching (and playing) drawings in motion in multiple mediums at the Center for New Media in downtown Kalamazoo. We will also have creative art projects for anyone who loves to draw and mini adventures throughout the year! Join us Wednesdays this fall from 11 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. in Room 65 at the Center for New Media. All students are welcome! For more information, contact Aubrey Rodgers at arodgers@kvcc.edu.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MW52cWVjYzlydXVtdXRqZm43bDA2dG9icGcgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>11:00 am TTC International Crafts Day</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 11:00 - 2026-11-18 01:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Join us for International Craft Day at the Texas Township Campus, a hands-on celebration of creativity and culture!<br><ul><li>TTC Craft Day, TTC Cafeteria Pit, 11 a.m. to 1 p.m.</li></ul>Explore diverse crafts, such as African paper beads, Thai string dolls and vibrant Portuguese azulejos. Drop in anytime to discover new skills and experience how crafting brings people together across cultures.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NGVkZmhqY3F0dm51NjY4cWhnYmUzdW1sb2UgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>12:00 pm Give Thanks for Strengths</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 12:00 - 2026-11-18 01:30</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">It's the season for gratitude! Tell someone that you are thankful for their strengths. Stop by and grab a free gratitude card and some treats. All are welcome to attend. Join us in lower level of the Cafeteria on the Texas Township Campus.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NW0zb3NkdTg3OTIwc2pyYjZvcWVrcmdram0gaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>3:00 pm Math Club Meeting</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 03:00 - 2026-11-18 05:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, Texas Township Campus</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><p>Fall in love with math! Join us from 3 - 5 p.m. for fun games, snacks and more! Meetings take place at the Texas Township Campus in the Student Lounge near the Learning Center. Take part on any of the following dates:</p><p></p><ul><li>Sept. 23 and 25</li><li>Oct. 28 and 30</li><li>Nov. 18 and 20</li><li>Dec. 2 and 4</li></ul><p></p><p>For questions, please email Lisa Winch at<a href=mailto:lwinch@kvcc.edu><u><u>lwinch@kvcc.edu</u></u></a>.</p></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MzIxNXAzYWttMTA3b2R0azdwMTY4bTIxMTEgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>3:30 pm Game Show Study Event</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-18 03:30 - 2026-11-18 05:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, Texas Township Campus</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><br>Need help passing your BIO 214 exams? These events are for you! Bring your notes, questions and a friend for some fun and interactive exam prep. Study for BIO 214 exams two through five, test your knowledge and have fun while studying! Join us in Room 2410 from 3:30 - 5 p.m. on any of the following dates:<br><ul><li>Wednesday, Oct. 14</li><li>Wednesday, Nov. 4</li><li>Wednesday, Nov. 18</li><li>Wednesday, Dec. 9</li></ul></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=N3V1cWpsZGNubjA5dGJkZHFuZnJjam5haTkgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Thursday, November 19</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>12:00 pm Gaming Club</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-19 12:00 - 2026-11-19 05:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">This organization is for students interested in playing all types of games. The club meets Thursdays this fall from noon to 5 p.m. at the Texas Township in Room 5740. For more information, contact Beth Brandon at ebrandon@kvcc.edu or Mary Cox at mcox@kvcc.edu.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MDlubnNlbTg1a284a2U2dHBuZDh0dnMxZnIgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>3:00 pm Global Gathering: International Education Week Reception</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-19 03:00 - 2026-11-19 05:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">As we closeout International Education Week, join us for an afternoon reception in Room 4240 at the Texas Township Campus. Enjoyconversation and cross-cultural connection while immersed in internationalmusic and art. Appetizers highlighting various global cuisines will also beserved.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NnM2Mm9wbWJoYWw5YmNnNWJsaTdtOWpkZWEgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>6:00 pm At Home Herbalism Class (Part 6 of 6)</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-19 06:00 - 2026-11-19 08:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Students will explore the impact of ancestral plants, sources of materia medica, ethical and sustainable foraging techniques and recipes for building a home apothecary. Engage in on-campus plant walks to discuss bioregional, cultivated and seasonal plants.<br>Food Innovation Center<br><br><b>*Note:</b>This is a six-week course. This is class six of six.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MW9mN3IzMHZxOWdmN21lOWFza3FuazMxY2FfUjIwMjYxMDIyVDIyMDAwMCBob25ianYyNG9na2c2NDl1ZGIwZDhraTRtMEBn" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Friday, November 20</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>3:00 pm Math Club Meeting</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-20 03:00 - 2026-11-20 05:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, Texas Township Campus</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><p>Fall in love with math! Join us from 3 - 5 p.m. for fun games, snacks and more! Meetings take place at the Texas Township Campus in the Student Lounge near the Learning Center. Take part on any of the following dates:</p><p></p><ul><li>Sept. 23 and 25</li><li>Oct. 28 and 30</li><li>Nov. 18 and 20</li><li>Dec. 2 and 4</li></ul><p></p><p>For questions, please email Lisa Winch at<a href=mailto:lwinch@kvcc.edu><u><u>lwinch@kvcc.edu</u></u></a>.</p></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MzIxNXAzYWttMTA3b2R0azdwMTY4bTIxMTEgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>3:30 pm Deadline to Submit for High School Art & Design Competition</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-20 03:30 - <br />
<b>Deprecated</b>:  strtotime(): Passing null to parameter #1 ($datetime) of type string is deprecated in <b>/srv/www/www.kvcc.edu/public/includes/sections/cougar-news-events.php</b> on line <b>166</b><br />
1969-12-31 07:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> </p>
						<p class="calendar-details">The deadline to submit artwork for the High School Art &amp; Design Competition is TODAY at 3:30 p.m. For more information or to submit, visit<a href=https://forms.gle/XsNNhCcr9kbYxopS7>https://forms.gle/XsNNhCcr9kbYxopS7</a>.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=M2liM2QxNmVsZDliNTNhdHBjNjFmMjJhMzEgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Saturday, November 21</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>10:00 am Introduction to Mobile Poultry Systems Class</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-21 10:00 - 2026-11-21 01:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">This course on mobile chicken management will provide chicken keepers with design tips and tricks to maximize poultry flock mobility, utility and contribution to the landscape. Course topics include the pros and cons of common mobile chicken infrastructure, including chicken tractors, mobile coops and electric fencing and security.<br>Food Innovation Center<br><br><b>Registration Fee:</b>$30<br><br><b>Register Here:</b><a href=https://www.campusce.net/kvcccommunity/course/course.aspx?catId=37>https://www.campusce.net/kvcccommunity/course/course.aspx?catId=37</a></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NmRoZW9tdTlhdmpyNWhubXBpbHZwdWthbzYgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>1:30 pm Garden Planning Vision Boards Class</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-21 01:30 - 2026-11-21 04:30</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Create a 2027 Garden vision board using seed catalogs, garden magazines, dried plant material and other ephemera! Participants will be offered prompts for planning their gardens and setting intentions for their growing spaces. Chat with other local gardeners and hear about what your Kalamazoo neighbors have planned for the next growing season!<br>Food Innovation Center<br><br><b>Registration Fee:</b>$30<br><br><b>Register Here:</b><a href=https://www.campusce.net/kvcccommunity/course/course.aspx?catId=37>https://www.campusce.net/kvcccommunity/course/course.aspx?catId=37</a></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MjlxamdvdnUwNm9qNGVvZmQzc2Qwcmw4OXQgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Monday, November 23</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>2:00 pm Thanksgiving Valley Food Share</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-23 02:00 - 2026-11-23 04:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><br>Valley Food Share is an initiative designed to meet the immediate food needs of Kalamazoo Valley students. Through the program, currently enrolled students can pick up a bag, or a share which includes food grown locally and sourced through our own Food Innovation Center as well as non-perishable items from Kalamazoo Loaves and Fishes. For more information, visit<a href=http://kvcc.edu/foodshare target=_blank><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>kvcc.edu/foodsh<u></u>are</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>This week's special Thanksgiving-themed food share will be distributed at the<b>Food Innovation Center parking lot</b>.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NjQzNDJkODVtOTQ3ajduaWVvdXFhcGdxNmcgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>6:00 pm Fire Academy Graduation</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-23 06:00 - 2026-11-23 07:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Groves Campus, 7107 Elm Valley Dr, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Support graduates from the Fire Academy during their winter graduation. The ceremony will be held on the Groves Campus in room 1020.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MG9vamJ1dGcya2ZnaHFmazkzZDhxajBidm0gaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                <p class="day-heading">Tuesday, November 24</p>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>11:00 am CRU Club</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-24 11:00 - 2026-11-24 12:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">CRU Club is a community of students who choose to experience God through Jesus. The club's goals are to make a positive impact in the world. CRU will meet this fall on Tuesdays at 11 a.m. near the Coffee Hut in the Student Commons at the Texas Township Campus. For more information, contact Amy Reynolds at <a href=mailto:areynolds2@kvcc.edu>areynolds2@kvcc.edu</a>or Nicole Popour at <a href=mailto:npopour@kvcc.edu>npopour@kvcc.edu</a>.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NnU1bmV2N2g1dGZ0Z2JtazZzNmlrbHFrNGUgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>2:00 pm Thanksgiving Valley Food Share</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-24 02:00 - 2026-11-24 04:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Community College, 6767 W O Ave, Kalamazoo, MI 49009, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><br>Valley Food Share is an initiative designed to meet the immediate food needs of Kalamazoo Valley students. Through the program, currently enrolled students can pick up a bag, or a share which includes food grown locally and sourced through our own Food Innovation Center as well as non-perishable items from Kalamazoo Loaves and Fishes. For more information, visit<a href=http://kvcc.edu/foodshare target=_blank><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>kvcc.edu/foodsh<u></u>are</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>.<br><br>This week's special Thanksgiving-themed share will be distributed outside the<b>Tower Entrance at Texas Township Campus</b>.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NmpsdHBzOXFtMGFnbTB1dWM2c24xbGEwN2wgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>5:00 pm Taps on Tuesdays</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-24 05:00 - 2026-11-24 07:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Kalamazoo Valley Culinary/Allied Health Building, 418 E Walnut St, Kalamazoo, MI 49007, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details"><p>Enjoy delicious beverages and food pairings at happy-hour-style events hosted by our culinary students and staff. All are welcome -- no reservations required!</p><p>Located at the Culinary and Allied Health Building.</p></p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=MWJoOW92Y3Bsc2traG9pMTRibzd0aGR2c2EgaG9uYmp2MjRvZ2tnNjQ5dWRiMGQ4a2k0bTBAZw==" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                                            <details>
                    <summary>6:00 pm Visible Mending Class (Part 8 of 8)</summary>

                    <!--<p>When: 2026-11-24 06:00 - 2026-11-24 08:00</p>-->
                    <p><strong>Where:</strong> Food Innovation Center, 224 E Crosstown Pkwy, Kalamazoo, MI 49001, USA</p>
						<p class="calendar-details">Transform your holey clothing into a work of slow fashion art! Repairing and refurbishing your clothing keeps your clothing out of the waste stream, saves you money, gives you a creative outlet and will make you the envy of your friends. Join us for this eight-week exploration into the world of mending. We will be learning mending of socks, jeans and other pants, shirts and more types of clothing using techniques of weaving, embroidery, knitting, and more. Minimal sewing skills are required- we'll teach you what you need to know although some familiarity is useful.<br>Food Innovation Center<br><br><b>*Note:</b>This is an eight-week class. This class is part eight of eight.</p>
						<a style="font-size: 0.9em;" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/event?eid=NHE1dmIzcmRlZ2VwZDRyZTFta3U2N2Q1aW9fUjIwMjYxMDEzVDIyMDAwMCBob25ianYyNG9na2c2NDl1ZGIwZDhraTRtMEBn" target="_blank">more details >></a><br><br>
                </details>
                    

    </div>
